  "facts": [
    "Opened 16 April 2000, the Domain Tunnel ran under the Yarra River, spanning 1.6 km with 460 m cut‑and‑cover, 680 m bored, and a 500 m shallow river crossing built while the river kept flowing.",
    "During the 23 March 2007 Burnley Tunnel disaster, evacuees used cross‑passage tunnels to exit into the Domain Tunnel, which remained open for westbound traffic and avoided a city‑wide gridlock.",
    "Engineers employed roadheaders for the bored section and a moving cofferdam at the eastern portal, allowing continuous river flow and a maximum depth of 40 m beneath Kings Domain."
